@nsobid-5CC7A76ED820CF4C45AA7B935C79307F

# THEATRHYTHM FINAL BAR LINE 1.0.5 - 3840x2160 resolution

// Theatrhythm Final Bar Line is a Unity title and renders at a native
// 1920x1080 when docked (1280x720 handheld).  Raising that takes three
// separate changes, all of which are in this file:
//
//   1. the resolution ScreenManagerNX hands to Screen.width/Screen.height
//      and to the NVN window crop,
//   2. the min(w,1920)/min(h,1080) ceiling inside RequestResolution, which
//      would otherwise clamp (1) straight back down to 1080p,
//   3. the fixed 1920x1080 the player allocates its back-buffer textures
//      and backbuffer RenderSurface at.  The NX player always allocates a
//      full 1080p surface and renders into a sub-rect of it, so without
//      this the frame is still rendered at 1080p no matter what (1) says.
//
// The back-buffer memory pool is sized from the texture storage sizes at
// runtime, so it grows with this patch on its own -- there is no fixed pool
// constant to enlarge.  Unity's own heap is taken from nn::os::QueryMemoryInfo
// at startup, so it scales with the emulator's DRAM Size setting too.

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces the render and scan-out resolution to 3840x2160
// (4.00x the pixels of the native 1920x1080).

@enabled
// 1. ScreenManagerNX: the docked/handheld resolution pair, at every site
//    that picks one (initial setup x2, operation-mode change,
//    performance-mode change).  Both halves of each pair are set to the
//    target, so the resolution no longer depends on dock state.
01314F1C 150E8152
01314F20 16E08152
01314F64 08E08152
01314F6C 080E8152
01314F80 08E08152
01314F88 080E8152
01315F28 160E8152
01315F2C 17E08152
01315F70 08E08152
01315F78 080E8152
01315F8C 08E08152
01315F94 080E8152
01260E18 08E08152
01260E1C 09E08152
01260E24 080E8152
01260E28 090E8152
01260E5C 08E08152
01260E60 09E08152
01260E68 080E8152
01260E6C 090E8152
// 2. ScreenManagerNX::RequestResolution ceiling (min with 1920x1080).
//    Raised so the values above survive; the surrounding compares are
//    untouched, so the clamp still behaves as a min() for any input.
012612CC 08E08152
012612DC 080E8152
// 3. The fixed 1080p allocations: the backbuffer RenderSurface and the
//    three NVN back-buffer textures plus the depth buffer (~127 MB total
//    at this resolution, against ~33 MB stock).  This is the change that
//    actually raises the internal render resolution rather than just
//    stretching a 1080p image.
01315FC8 030E8152
01315FD0 02E08152
0132FFE4 190E8152
0132FFEC 01E08152
01330088 01E08152
01330248 020E8152
01330250 01E08152
@stop

// Reverse-engineered against the Unity NX player in main (build id above).
// Every offset here was located by signature and byte-verified.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-visuen-mods
